    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m curious about making a really good cup of coffee. What are the key things to keep in mind?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To make a really good cup of coffee, keep these key factors in mind:\n\n1. **Quality Beans**: Use freshly roasted coffee beans instead of pre-ground coffee. Look for beans from different regions to explore unique flavors.\n\n2. **Proper Grinding**: Grind your beans just before brewing to preserve their flavor and aroma. The grind size should match your brewing method.\n\n3. **Water Quality**: Use cold, filtered water to avoid any unpleasant tastes from tap water. The ideal brewing temperature is between 195-205\u00b0F (90-96\u00b0C).\n\n4. **Coffee-to-Water Ratio**: A common ratio is about 1:15 (1 gram of coffee for every 15 grams of water). Adjust based on your taste preference.\n\n5. **Brewing Method**: Choose a method that allows for control over the brewing process, like pour-over or a quality drip coffee maker. Ensure that your equipment is clean and prepped before use.\n\n6. **Steeping Time**: Pay attention to the steeping time, as it can affect the flavor. Consistency in all these factors will help you recreate your perfect cup.\n\nExperiment with these",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0042-97-14786:3": 3.9616641998291016,
            "clueweb22-en0011-12-12454:10": 3.145866870880127,
