      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "There are four main types of coffee beans, each with unique characteristics:\n\n1. **Arabica**: This is the most common type, making up about 60% of global coffee production. Arabica beans are known for their sweet, fruity flavors and bright acidity. They thrive in high altitudes and are often found in specialty coffees.\n\n2. **Robusta**: Comprising most of the remaining coffee production, Robusta beans are hardier and more resistant to pests. They contain more caffeine than Arabica, leading to a stronger, more bitter taste. Robusta is often used in instant coffee and espresso blends.\n\n3. **Liberica**: This is a rarer type, accounting for only about 2% of the world's coffee supply. Liberica beans have a unique flavor profile, sometimes described as smoky or floral, and are primarily produced in Malaysia and the Philippines.\n\n4. **Excelsa**: Often considered a variety of Liberica, Excelsa has a tart, fruity taste and is mainly grown in Southeast Asia. It combines attributes of both light and dark roast coffees.\n\nEach type of bean offers distinct flavors and brewing qualities, so exploring them can enhance your coffee experience!",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0003-90-16104:1": 3.298487663269043,
            "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:0": 3.0595455169677734,
            "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:1": 2.805636167526245,
            "clueweb22-en0022-34-09790:7": 2.776280164718628,
