    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm curious about making good coffee. Any tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To make a great cup of coffee, start with high-quality, freshly roasted beans and grind them just before brewing to preserve their flavor. Use filtered or spring water heated to about 200\u00b0F (93\u00b0C) for optimal extraction. The brewing method matters too\u2014try a pour-over for a clean, flavorful cup or a French press for a richer taste. Keep your equipment clean to avoid any off flavors. Since you love starting your day with coffee, experimenting with these tips could make your mornings even better!",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0036-57-16124:15": 12.310099601745605,
            "clueweb22-en0046-47-02643:0": 12.092900276184082,
            "clueweb22-en0010-72-05312:2": 11.84529972076416
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I get grumpy if I don't get my coffee.",
            "I start my day by drinking coffee."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "There are four main types of coffee beans: Arabica, Robusta, Liberica, and Excelsa. Arabica is the most popular, making up about 60% of global coffee production. It\u2019s known for its smooth, sweet flavor with hints of fruit and sugar. Robusta, on the other hand, has a stronger, more bitter taste and higher caffeine content, making it ideal for espresso blends. Liberica beans are less common and have a unique, smoky flavor with floral and fruity notes. Excelsa, often considered a variety of Liberica, is known for its tart, fruity profile and is used to add complexity to blends. Since you enjoy starting your day with coffee, exploring these bean types could be a fun way to discover new flavors for your morning brew!",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:0": 16.188400268554688
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I start my day by drinking coffee."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans differ in both caffeine content and shape. Excelsa beans have a lower caffeine content, ranging from about 0.86 to 1.13 g per 100 g, while Liberica beans contain slightly more, at approximately 1.23 g per 100 g. In terms of shape, Liberica beans are larger and almond-shaped, whereas Excelsa beans are smaller and rounder. Despite Excelsa being classified as a variety of Liberica, these distinctions highlight their unique characteristics.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:6": 35.214900970458984,
            "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:12": 32.76089859008789
          },
