            "I start my day by drinking coffee.",
            "I occasionally experience mild acid reflux and prefer beverages that are gentle on the stomach."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that sounds good. What is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Roasting significantly impacts the taste of coffee by altering its chemical and physical properties. Lighter roasts retain more of the bean\u2019s intrinsic flavors, often resulting in brighter, fruitier, and more acidic profiles. Medium roasts balance the bean\u2019s natural flavors with the caramelization of sugars, offering a smoother and more rounded taste. Dark roasts, on the other hand, emphasize bold, smoky, and chocolatey notes, with reduced acidity. Since you prefer beverages gentle on the stomach, a medium roast might be a good choice, as it offers a balanced flavor without the intense acidity of lighter roasts or the bitterness of darker ones. Experimenting with roast levels could help you find the perfect match for your morning coffee ritual.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0041-01-05927:10": 19.43400001525879
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
