        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m trying to learn how to make a good cup of coffee. Where should I start?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To make a good cup of coffee at home, begin with a simple brewing method such as French Press, AeroPress, or pour-over, which are affordable and easy for beginners to master [DOC-1][DOC-2]. The most important factor is using fresh, good-quality coffee beans, as even the best technique can't compensate for stale or low-quality beans [DOC-1]. Guides and cookbooks, like those from Blue Bottle Coffee, offer step-by-step instructions and recipes to help you explore different brewing styles and flavors [DOC-4]. Don't hesitate to ask your local barista for advice or try different beans and methods to discover what you enjoy most. Since you occasionally experience mild acid reflux, you might want to experiment with brewing methods that produce a smoother, less acidic cup, such as cold brew or using darker roasts [DOC-2]. Are you interested in learning about coffee machines or manual brewing methods?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0013-94-17771:0": 0.03009207275993712,
            "clueweb22-en0020-62-14086:0": 0.02761904761904762,
