          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that's helpful! What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Coffee beans come from four main species: Arabica, Robusta, Liberica, and Excelsa. Arabica beans account for about 60% of global coffee production and are prized for their sweeter, more complex flavors and bright acidity, making them popular in specialty coffee and pour-over brewing [DOC-2][DOC-3]. Robusta beans are more bitter, have higher caffeine content, and are often used in espresso blends for their strong flavor and crema [DOC-1][DOC-3]. Liberica beans are less common, known for their unique, fruity, and floral notes, while Excelsa (a sub-species of Liberica) offers tart, fruity flavors and is sometimes used to add complexity to blends [DOC-3]. For most home brewers, starting with Arabica beans is recommended for their approachable flavor and versatility [DOC-2]. How do I choose the best coffee beans for my taste preferences?",
