          "text": "Excelsa coffee beans typically contain between 0.86 to 1.13g of caffeine per 100g, which is slightly lower than Liberica beans, which average around 1.23g per 100g [clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:6][clueweb22-en0022-85-00226:7]. In terms of shape, Liberica beans are distinctively almond-shaped, whereas Excelsa beans are smaller, rounder, and asymmetrical, averaging about 9mm long and 6mm wide [clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:6][clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:4]. Despite their similarities and shared classification under Coffea liberica, these physical and chemical differences set them apart. Are you interested in brewing tips for these less common coffee beans?",
