          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yes, tell me more! Does brewing affect bitterness and acidity in coffee?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of brewing on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Brewing methods play a major role in the final taste of your coffee. Cold brew is especially gentle on the stomach, reducing acidity by up to 70% compared to hot brewing, and resulting in a smoother, less bitter cup\u2014making it ideal for those with acid reflux or sensitivity [clueweb22-en0016-51-04615:1][clueweb22-en0008-91-12781:11]. French press brewing also produces a smoother cup with less perceived bitterness than drip or espresso, as the grounds steep longer and more natural oils are retained [clueweb22-en0006-16-13801:13]. Drip (pour-over) methods can bring out more acidity and brightness, but adjusting grind size (using medium-fine rather than fine) and water temperature can help reduce bitterness [clueweb22-en0018-17-14357:4]. Clean equipment and filtered water also help minimize unwanted bitterness and acidity [clueweb22-en0006-16-13801:13].",
