          "text": "For high-quality coffee at home, start by using fresh, high-quality beans and grinding them just before brewing. Precision matters: using a scale to measure both coffee and water ensures the ideal ratio and consistency, which many modern machines and pour-over setups now support [DOC-4][DOC-5]. Manual brewing methods like French Press, Chemex, or pour-over allow you to control variables such as water temperature, bloom cycle, and brew strength, resulting in a richer flavor [DOC-2][DOC-4]. If you want guidance, there are apps designed for coffee enthusiasts that offer step-by-step instructions, timers, and recipes tailored to your equipment [DOC-3]. For those with sensitive stomachs or mild acid reflux, consider using brewing methods that produce a smoother, less acidic cup, such as cold brew or certain pour-over techniques [DOC-1]. Would you like specific recommendations for coffee beans or equipment?",
