        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Hold on\u2014what does roasting do to coffee flavor?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Roasting is the key process that shapes coffee's flavor profile. Light roasts have a prominent toasted grain taste and higher acidity, preserving more of the bean's original flavors. Medium roasts offer a balanced flavor, while medium-dark roasts introduce spicier and sweeter notes. Dark roasts lose much of the original coffee flavor, instead developing bold, smoky, and sometimes bitter characteristics, with significantly reduced acidity and caffeine content [clueweb22-en0005-97-02617][clueweb22-en0016-38-10083]. Chemically, roasting causes the breakdown of sugars, proteins, and acids, and the formation of hundreds of new compounds responsible for coffee's aroma and taste. The process also reduces chlorogenic acids, which are linked to acidity, making dark roasts gentler on sensitive stomachs [clueweb22-en0038-74-03944][clueweb22-en0001-58-05338]. Are you interested in how to roast coffee beans at home?",
