          "text": "While all coffee beans contain some acidity, dark roast beans tend to be the least acidic, making them a better choice for those with acid reflux or sensitive stomachs [clueweb22-en0017-76-18714]. Additionally, there are specialty low-acid coffee beans and brands\u2014such as Tyler\u2019s No Acid Organic Ground Coffee and Puroast Low Acid Ground Coffee\u2014that are specifically processed to reduce acidity and are recommended for people with acid reflux or digestive sensitivities [clueweb22-en0040-46-06475][clueweb22-en0041-15-00331]. The acidity of coffee also depends on factors like the bean's origin, roast level, and brewing method, so choosing a dark roast or a brand marketed as 'low acid' is your best bet for a gentler cup [clueweb22-en0041-15-00331]. Are you interested in brewing methods that further reduce coffee acidity?",
