          "text": "Cold brewing coffee significantly lowers its acidity compared to hot brewing methods, making it gentler on the stomach\u2014even when using beans that are naturally higher in acid. The Toddy cold brew system is specifically recommended for people with acid reflux, as it produces a smooth, low-acid concentrate [clueweb22-en0026-27-09966][clueweb22-en0021-14-03799]. Additionally, using dark roast beans instead of light or medium roasts further decreases the acid content in your coffee [clueweb22-en0003-60-13479]. For the lowest acidity, combine dark roast beans with a cold brew method, and consider single-cup preparation for maximum freshness and minimal irritation [clueweb22-en0026-27-09966]. Are you interested in specific low-acid coffee brands or bean recommendations?",
