          "user_utterance": "I want to know how to make really good coffee. Any tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Start by using clean equipment and fresh coffee beans, ideally measured by weight for consistency. The grind size should match your brewing method\u2014coarse for a French press, medium for drip, and fine for espresso. Use filtered or spring water heated to about 200\u00b0F (93\u00b0C) for optimal extraction. The general rule is two tablespoons (10 grams) of ground coffee per six ounces (180 milliliters) of water. Avoid over-extraction by not using too fine a grind or too few grounds, as this can make your coffee bitter. Investing in quality filters and experimenting with different brewing methods, like a coffee press, can also enhance flavor. Finally, you can add steamed milk or flavorings to suit your taste [clueweb22-en0036-57-16124:15][clueweb22-en0028-86-13869:0][clueweb22-en0028-86-13869:1][clueweb22-en0038-81-03595:1]. Would you like recommendations for specific coffee beans or brewing equipment?",
