          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Actually, what are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Arabica beans are the most popular, making up about 60% of global coffee production. They are known for their sweeter, more complex flavors and bright acidity, making them ideal for pour-over and specialty coffees. Robusta beans are more robust and bitter, with higher caffeine content, and are often used in espresso blends for their strong flavor and crema. Liberica beans are less common, producing larger beans with a unique, somewhat fruity and floral flavor profile. Excelsa, a sub-species of Liberica, offers a tart, fruity taste and is often used to add complexity to blends. While Arabica and Robusta dominate the market, Liberica and Excelsa provide unique options for adventurous coffee drinkers [clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:0][clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:1][clueweb22-en0001-20-10010:19][clueweb22-en0013-60-07405:2]. Do you want recommendations for specific brands or origins of coffee beans?",
