          "user_utterance": "Maybe later. Now, what is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The roasting process transforms coffee beans both physically and chemically. Light roasts retain more of the bean's original acidity and unique flavors, resulting in a brighter, more complex cup. As beans are roasted longer and hotter, their acidity decreases and bitterness increases, with dark roasts developing pronounced roasted, nutty, or chocolatey flavors and sometimes a heavier mouthfeel [clueweb22-en0019-32-08323:4][clueweb22-en0017-74-02295:3]. During roasting, bean density drops, oils may migrate to the surface (especially in dark roasts), and volatile compounds responsible for aroma and flavor are released or transformed [clueweb22-en0041-01-05927:10][clueweb22-en0041-01-05927:9]. The choice of roast level thus has a major impact on the final taste, aroma, and even how gentle the coffee is on your stomach. Are you interested in how brewing methods interact with roast level?",
