          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "To keep your coffee beans fresh\u2014and your morning cup gentle on your stomach\u2014follow these evidence-based storage tips:\n\n**Best Practices for Storing Coffee Beans:**\n- **Airtight Containers:** Use opaque, airtight containers (like mason jars with tight lids) to keep out air, moisture, and light. This preserves flavor and prevents staleness.\n- **Cool, Dark Location:** Store beans in a pantry or cupboard away from heat sources (not on the counter or near the stove). Avoid sunlight and humidity.\n- **Buy Small, Use Fresh:** Purchase smaller amounts of beans more frequently. Beans are at peak freshness for about a month after roasting.\n- **Don\u2019t Freeze or Refrigerate:** Freezing can introduce moisture and degrade flavor; room temperature is best if you use beans within a month.\n\n**Why This Matters for You:**  \nProper storage keeps low-acid, specialty beans (like Lifeboost or Volcanica) at their best\u2014ensuring your coffee remains smooth, flavorful, and easy on your stomach, supporting your weight-loss and wellness goals.\n\nWould you like tips",
