          "user_utterance": "Yes, which containers are best for storing cold brew?",
          "user_rubrik": "Which one of Liberica and Excelsa is better for me?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For storing cold brew concentrate that\u2019s gentle on your stomach and supports your weight-loss goals, glass airtight containers are the gold standard:\n\n**Best Container Choices**\n- **Glass Jars or Pitchers:** Glass is non-porous, won\u2019t absorb odors or flavors, and preserves the smooth, low-acid profile of your coffee (ideal for acid reflux). Mason jars or glass bottles with tight lids work perfectly.\n- **Small, Individual Glass Containers:** Dividing concentrate into smaller jars reduces air exposure, slowing oxidation and keeping your coffee fresher, longer.\n- **Avoid Plastic:** Plastic can transfer unwanted flavors and isn\u2019t fully airtight, which can degrade taste and freshness.\n\n**Extra Tips**\n- Always seal containers tightly and refrigerate immediately.\n- For longer storage or convenience, freeze cold brew in ice cube trays\u2014just thaw cubes as needed.\n\nWould you like recommendations for specific brands or types of glass containers?",
