      {
        "turn": 13,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for the info! How about any potential downsides of cold brew coffee?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Drinking cold brew coffee in the morning offers benefits for weight loss and is generally gentler on the stomach, but there are a few potential downsides to consider\u2014especially given your mild acid reflux and preference for gentle beverages:\n\n**Potential Downsides of Cold Brew Coffee:**\n\n- **Still Acidic:** While cold brew is less acidic than hot coffee, it can still stimulate stomach acid production. Drinking it on an empty stomach may increase the risk of bloating, heartburn, or acid reflux\u2014even with low-acid beans (clueweb22-en0023-10-09135, clueweb22-en0033-12-02972, clueweb22-en0016-67-12268).\n- **Digestive Discomfort:** Some people experience bloating or indigestion from coffee, regardless of brew method. This is more likely if consumed without food (clueweb22-en0016-11-10221, clueweb22-en0034-30-18780).\n- **Caffeine Sensitivity:** Caffeine can relax the muscle between the stomach and esophagus,",
