          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of brewing on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 1,
          "text": "To enjoy cold brew while minimizing acid reflux and digestive discomfort\u2014especially given your weight-loss and sugar-free goals\u2014use these evidence-based strategies:\n\n**How to Mitigate Cold Brew Downsides**\n\n- **Never Drink on an Empty Stomach:** Always pair your cold brew with a light, protein-rich breakfast (like eggs or a low-sugar protein bar). This buffers stomach acid and reduces the risk of heartburn or bloating (clueweb22-en0023-10-09135, clueweb22-en0032-74-00428, clueweb22-en0040-35-06701).\n- **Choose Low-Acid, Dark Roast Beans:** Beans grown at low altitudes and dark roasts are gentler on digestion and less likely to trigger reflux (clueweb22-en0032-74-00428, clueweb22-en0001-32-10697).\n- **Opt for Decaf or Lower-Caffeine Options:** If caffeine is a trigger, try decaf or blend regular with decaf to reduce stomach irritation (clueweb22-en0032",
