          "text": "For your goals\u2014weight loss, sugar-free, and gentle on the stomach\u2014these brewing methods work best with low-acid, medium roast Arabica beans (like Kona, Volcanica Low Acid, or LifeBoost):\n\n**Top Brewing Methods:**\n\n- **Cold Brew:**  \n  - Extracts less acid, making coffee smoother and easier on digestion.  \n  - Ideal for minimizing acid reflux and maximizing flavor from low-acid beans.  \n  - Works well with single-origin beans from Brazil, Sumatra, Kona, and specialty low-acid blends.  \n  - Simple: steep coarsely ground beans in cold water for 12\u201318 hours, then strain.\n\n- **French Press:**  \n  - Produces a rich, full-bodied cup that highlights the smooth, chocolatey, or caramel notes of low-acid beans.  \n  - Use a coarse grind and steep for 4\u20135 minutes.\n\n- **Drip or Pour-Over:**  \n  - Clean, balanced flavor\u2014especially with medium-coarse grind.  \n  - Good for daily routines and easy to",
