          "text": "Here\u2019s a step-by-step guide for making cold brew coffee that\u2019s gentle on your stomach, sugar-free, and weight-loss friendly:\n\n**1. Use the Right Beans**\n- Choose low-acid, medium roast Arabica beans (e.g., Lifeboost, Volcanica Low Acid, Kona). These are smoother and less likely to trigger acid reflux.\n\n**2. Grind Coarse**\n- Grind beans coarsely just before brewing. This maximizes smoothness and minimizes bitterness.\n\n**3. Coffee-to-Water Ratio**\n- Use a 1:15 ratio (e.g., 1 cup coarsely ground coffee to 15 cups cold, filtered water).\n\n**4. Steep**\n- Combine grounds and water in a glass container.\n- Stir gently, cover, and refrigerate for 12\u201318 hours (longer steeping = smoother, less acidic).\n\n**5. Strain**\n- Use a fine mesh sieve, cheesecloth, or coffee filter to strain out grounds.\n\n**6. Serve**\n- Dilute concentrate with water or ice to taste. Drink",
