          "text": "Cold brew concentrate stays fresh in the fridge for up to 2 weeks if kept undiluted and refrigerated immediately after brewing. For best flavor and smoothness (important for your sensitive stomach and weight-loss goals), use it within the first week\u2014after that, taste and aroma start to fade. \n\nKey tips:\n- Only store the pure concentrate; adding milk or sweeteners shortens shelf life to just 8 hours.\n- Always check for signs of spoilage (off smell, mold near the lid).\n- Cold brew\u2019s low acidity and natural sweetness mean you won\u2019t need sugar, supporting your dietary preferences.\n\nWould you like advice on the best containers for storing your cold brew?",
