          "text": "Given your goals\u2014sugar-free, weight-loss friendly, and gentle on the stomach\u2014here are the best alternative coffee brewing methods to explore beyond cold brew:\n\n**1. French Press**\n- Produces a rich, smooth cup that highlights the natural flavors of low-acid beans.\n- Use a coarse grind and steep for 4\u20135 minutes.\n- No need for sugar or creamers; preserves antioxidants and is easy on digestion.\n\n**2. Pour-Over (e.g., Chemex)**\n- Clean, balanced flavor with minimal bitterness.\n- Use a medium-coarse grind and a 1:15 coffee-to-water ratio.\n- Chemex filters remove more oils and acids, making it gentler for acid reflux.\n\n**3. Flash Brew (Japanese Iced Coffee)**\n- Hot coffee brewed directly over ice, preserving delicate flavors and reducing bitterness.\n- Less acidic than traditional hot coffee, often enjoyed black or with a splash of non-dairy milk.\n\n**4. Dedicated Low-Acid Hot Brew**\n- Use dark roast, low-acid beans with drip or single-serve",
