      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! What impact does roasting have on the coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Roasting has a significant impact on the taste of coffee. The way the beans are roasted can bring out or overshadow the unique flavors of the coffee. Lighter roasts tend to preserve the coffee's natural acidity, while darker roasts can produce a bolder, more bitter taste. The roasting process can also enhance or reduce certain flavor characteristics, such as sweetness, body, and fruit notes, depending on the roast level and technique used. Ultimately, the roast level can greatly affect the overall flavor profile of the coffee.",
