          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yeah, that\u2019s true! But I want tips on actually making the coffee better. Any tricks with beans, water, or maybe different methods? I prefer options gentle on the stomach.",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To make good coffee, start by using fresh, high-quality coffee beans. Consider grinding your own beans just before brewing to ensure the freshest flavor. Use filtered or distilled water to prevent any impurities or metals from affecting the taste. As for brewing methods, you may want to try a French press or a pour-over, which can produce a smoother, less acidic coffee that's gentle on the stomach. Additionally, opt for a lighter roast, as it tends to be easier to digest than darker roasts. Experiment with different methods and ratios to find the perfect balance for your taste preferences.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0035-48-11701:8": 2.5740108489990234,
