          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, pour-over sounds good. Should I grind Liberica beans coarsely or finely for a pour-over?",
          "user_rubrik": "Which one of Liberica and Excelsa is better for me?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For a pour-over, it's best to use a medium-coarse to medium-fine grind. This will allow for the right amount of extraction and bring out the unique flavor profile of the Liberica beans. If the grind is too coarse, the coffee may taste weak or watery, while a grind that's too fine can result in a bitter taste. You can adjust the grind size based on your personal taste preferences and the specific pour-over method you're using. A cone-shaped pour-over, for example, may require a slightly finer grind. Experiment with different grind sizes to find the perfect balance for your Liberica pour-over.",
