      {
        "turn": 10,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Savory is perfect\u2014maybe I\u2019ll try eggs and some dark chocolate on the side! Could you tell me how roasting impacts the flavor for Liberica beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Roasting can significantly impact the flavor of Liberica beans. Lighter roasts tend to preserve the unique, smoky or woody notes of Liberica, while darker roasts can bring out a richer, more full-bodied flavor. However, darker roasts may also increase the acidity, which could be a concern for you given your acid reflux. A medium roast might be a good balance, as it can enhance the flavor without overpowering the unique characteristics of Liberica beans. Experimenting with different roast levels can help you find the perfect flavor profile that suits your taste preferences.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0041-11-10311:4": 5.553825378417969,
            "clueweb22-en0013-79-17659:4": 4.580116271972656,
