      {
        "turn": 11,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense. What about the brewing process itself\u2014how does it affect the final taste of the coffee?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of brewing on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The brewing process can significantly impact the final taste of the coffee. Factors such as the amount of time the coffee is allowed to steep, the temperature of the water, and the ratio of coffee to water can all affect the flavor. For example, if the coffee is steeped for too long, it can become bitter, while too little steeping time can result in a weak or under-extracted flavor. Additionally, the brewing method itself, such as pour-over, French press, or drip brewing, can also influence the flavor profile of the coffee. In the case of Liberica beans, a pour-over or French press method can help bring out their unique flavor characteristics. Experimenting with different brewing parameters can help you find the optimal balance for your taste preferences.",
