        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s a bit more helpful! I usually use a French press, though. Any advice on making especially good coffee with my French press? Also, which coffee beans are easiest on the stomach?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "For a great French press coffee, use freshly roasted and ground coffee beans, and adjust the steeping time to your liking. Darker roasts tend to work well with French press. As for stomach-friendly coffee beans, look for Arabica beans, which are naturally lower in acidity and easier to digest. You can also try a medium to dark roast, as they tend to be smoother on the stomach. Experiment with different beans and roasts to find the one that works best for you. And don't forget to clean your French press regularly to prevent any buildup of old coffee oils.",
