      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for the summary. I\u2019ve also come across \u201cExcelsa\u201d beans\u2014how do Excelsa and Liberica compare, both in caffeine content and their shape?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans have some differences. Excelsa beans are smaller and rounder in shape, whereas Liberica beans are larger and have an irregular shape, often compared to an almond. In terms of caffeine content, Excelsa beans generally have lower caffeine levels, ranging from 0.86 to 1.13g per 100g, compared to Liberica. Excelsa beans also have a unique flavor profile, with fruity and tart notes, and are often used in blends to add complexity.",
