      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Makes sense. How does roasting affect the taste of coffee overall?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Roasting plays a significant role in shaping the flavor and aroma of coffee. It breaks down chlorogenic acid into caffeic and quinic acid, which contribute to bitterness and astringency. The level of roasting, whether light, medium, or dark, can greatly impact the flavor profile, with darker roasts tend to be smoother and less acidic. Roasting also brings out the unique flavors and aromas of the coffee beans, making each roast level distinct. As someone who prefers a gentle coffee, a medium to dark roast might be a good option for you.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0021-26-17141:1": 4.407517910003662,
