          "text": "Excelsa coffee beans have a lower caffeine content compared to Liberica coffee beans. While Liberica coffee beans have a caffeine content of 2.2 to 2.7g per 100g, Excelsa coffee beans have a caffeine content of 0.86 to 1.13g per 100g. In terms of shape, both Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans have an almond-like shape, but Excelsa beans are smaller and rounder compared to the larger and more irregularly shaped Liberica beans. This difference in shape and size can affect the flavor and aroma of the coffee. Excelsa coffee beans are known for their fruity and tart flavor, while Liberica coffee beans have a unique aroma and a smoky taste. The shape and size of the coffee beans can also impact the brewing process and the final flavor of the coffee. Therefore, the choice between Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans will depend on personal preference and the desired flavor profile",
