          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Certainly! Both Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans come from the same species group but have notable differences.   **Caffeine content:**   Liberica beans generally have slightly less caffeine than Robusta but more than Arabica, typically around 1.2% caffeine by weight. Excelsa beans tend to have caffeine levels somewhat similar to Liberica, sometimes a bit lower or comparable, but exact amounts vary depending on cultivation.  **Shape and size:**   Liberica beans are larger and more irregular in shape compared to Arabica and Robusta, often described as elongated with a somewhat asymmetrical form. They have a distinctive, uneven surface texture. Excelsa beans are smaller than Liberica but still larger than Arabica, with a more rounded shape and a slightly wrinkled surface. Both are quite distinct from the more uniform and oval Arabica beans.  In summary, Liberica beans are larger and more irregular, Excelsa smaller and rounder, and both have moderate caffeine levels, fitting your interest in unique flavors with balanced strength.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
