      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That helps. I already have a cooking machine, but I\u2019m thinking of something specifically for coffee. Any recommendations for coffee makers that are gentle on the stomach\u2014maybe ones that highlight low-acid brewing?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "As someone who experiences mild acid reflux, you'll want a coffee maker that uses a low-acid brewing method. Consider a pour-over or a French press, as they tend to produce coffee with lower acidity. Alternatively, look for coffee makers with a built-in water filter or a machine that uses a cold brew method, which can also reduce acidity. Some popular brands that offer low-acid brewing options include Chemex and Toddy. These machines can help you achieve a smooth and rich cup of coffee that's gentle on your stomach.",
