          "text": "Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans have distinct characteristics. Excelsa beans have a higher caffeine content compared to Liberica, with around 1.5-2% caffeine. Liberica beans, on the other hand, have a lower caffeine content, around 1-1.5%. In terms of shape, Excelsa beans are often irregular and elongated, while Liberica beans are larger and have a distinctive shape with a distinctive \"hook\" at the tip. These unique characteristics set them apart from other coffee bean varieties, like Arabica and Robusta. As someone who starts their day with coffee, you might find it interesting to experiment with these lesser-known beans to find your perfect cup.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
