      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, thanks! Cold brew sounds promising. Could you give me a simple recipe for making cold brew at home? I have a few different grinders and I\u2019m curious about grind size too.",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a smooth, stomach-gentle cold brew, use a coarse to extra-coarse grind, similar to ground peppercorns. This prevents over-extraction during the long steeping time. A good starting ratio is 1:8 coffee to cold water (e.g., 40g coffee to 320ml water). Combine the grounds and water, then steep in the fridge for 12-24 hours. Afterwards, strain the concentrate and dilute it to your preference. Since you have grinders, a burr grinder is recommended for consistent particle size, which helps achieve optimal flavor.",
