      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks! Are there any other lesser-known types of coffee beans I should know about if I want to try something different?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Beyond Arabica and Robusta, you could explore lesser-known types like Liberica, known for its unique fruity, floral, and smoky notes. It's also quite rare. Another option is Excelsa, which offers a tart flavor profile, a mix of light and dark roast characteristics, and is also rare and sought-after. You might also consider Barako, a well-known type in the Philippines.",
          "citations": {
