          "user_utterance": "Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Excelsa beans generally have a lower caffeine content, ranging from 0.86 to 1.13g per 100g. Liberica beans have a slightly higher caffeine content, around 1.23g per 100g.\n\nRegarding shape, Liberica beans are typically larger, almond-shaped, and often irregular or asymmetrical with a characteristic \"hook\" at the tip. Excelsa beans are described as smaller and rounder, or asymmetrical, and can have a highly variable shape.",
