          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Which one of Liberica and Excelsa is better for me?",
          "user_rubrik": "Which one of Liberica and Excelsa is better for me?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Given your preference for smooth, stomach-gentle coffee, Liberica would likely be a more suitable choice than Excelsa. Excelsa beans are characterized by a \"tart acidity\" (Passages 3, 17), which might not be ideal for acid reflux.\n\nLiberica, on the other hand, offers unique floral, fruity, smoky, and woody notes (Passages 2, 4, 6, 16). While Liberica has a slightly higher caffeine content (around 1.23g per 100g) compared to Excelsa (around 1g per 100g) (Passage 1), its flavor profile does not explicitly mention high acidity, making it potentially gentler for your stomach.",
