        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m looking for ways to make really good coffee. Any suggestions on where to start?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "To make high-quality, stomach-gentle coffee, consider starting with darker roasts or low-acid beans like those from Mexico or Sumatra. Cold brew is an excellent method as it produces lower acid concentrations. You can also try adding a pinch of baking soda or some almond milk to your brew to neutralize acidity. Opting for decaf or half-caf can also help reduce potential reflux triggers.",
