      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s interesting\u2014didn\u2019t know about the baking soda trick! Can you recommend brewing methods that bring out the best flavor but are also gentle on the stomach? I usually drink coffee first thing in the morning so smoothness is important.",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "For a smooth, flavorful, and stomach-gentle coffee, consider Cold Brew, which extracts fewer acidic compounds and results in a less bitter, fuller-flavored drink. The Toddy method is also excellent for acid reflux, as it's a cold water extract that reduces oils. Additionally, the Chemex pour-over system is known for producing a deliciously smooth, sweet-tasting brew by filtering out bitter notes.",
          "citations": {
