      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Those are some unique options! What are the main types of coffee beans out there, though? I want to understand the basics before picking.",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "The two main types of coffee beans are Arabica and Robusta.\n\n**Arabica** beans are widely preferred for their sweeter, softer, and more nuanced flavors, often with fruity or floral notes. They generally contain less caffeine and are considered smoother and higher quality, making them a good choice for stomach-gentle coffee.\n\n**Robusta** beans have a stronger, bolder, and often more bitter or earthy taste. They contain significantly higher caffeine (nearly double Arabica's) and more chlorogenic acids, which contribute to their harsher flavor. Robusta is often used in blends or instant coffee.",
          "citations": {
