      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s more helpful, thanks. What\u2019s the easiest way to make a good cold brew at home?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "The easiest way to make good cold brew at home is typically the immersion method. Simply combine coarse coffee grounds with cold water in a pitcher or mason jar, then let it steep in the refrigerator overnight for about 12-15 hours. Another very convenient option is to use a French press, which simplifies the straining process as it has a built-in filter. After steeping, just strain the coffee to remove the grounds. Cold brew is naturally less acidic, making it a stomach-friendly choice.",
