          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Excelsa beans generally have lower caffeine content, ranging from 0.86 to 1.13g per 100g, while Liberica beans contain about 1.23g per 100g. Regarding shape, Liberica beans are typically almond-shaped and can be large and irregularly asymmetric. Excelsa beans are often described as smaller and rounder, though they can also be asymmetrical and vary in size.",
