        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019ll keep that in mind, thanks! Back to roasting\u2014what\u2019s the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Roasting drastically transforms green coffee beans, developing unique flavors and aromas through complex chemical reactions like the Maillard reaction and caramelization. This process creates compounds responsible for sweetness, fruity acidity, and body.\n\nThe roast level significantly impacts taste:\n*   **Light roasts** retain more of the bean's natural acidity and floral/fruity notes.\n*   **Darker roasts** generally have reduced acidity but can develop increased bitterness, often described as bittersweet, caramelized, or \"roastier.\" This bitterness stems from the breakdown of chlorogenic acids. Roasting also affects the coffee's body and activates oils, contributing to the overall flavor profile.",
