        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! Is there a particular coffee bean variety or roast level that works best for cold brew and is gentle on the stomach?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "For a smooth, low-acidity cold brew that's gentle on your stomach, focus on dark roasted coffee beans, as they naturally contain lower acid levels. Regarding bean varieties, those from origins like Mexico, Sumatra, Brazil, Peru, Guatemala, and Indonesia are known for their naturally lower acidity. Opting for Arabica beans over Robusta can also contribute to a less acidic cup.",
