      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s very helpful! Are there actually big differences in taste between Arabica and Robusta beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Yes, there are significant taste differences. Arabica beans are generally known for a sweeter, softer, and more complex flavor profile, often with notes of sugar, fruit, and berries, and a higher acidity. This is due to their higher sugar and lipid content. In contrast, Robusta beans typically have a bolder, harsher, and more bitter taste, often described as earthy, woody, or having a peanut aftertaste. Their higher caffeine and chlorogenic acid content contribute to this bitterness.",
