      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Excelsa coffee beans generally have a lower caffeine content, ranging from 0.86 to 1.13g per 100g. Liberica beans have a slightly higher caffeine concentration at 1.23g per 100g.\n\nRegarding shape, Liberica beans are typically larger and almond-shaped, often described as irregular or asymmetrical with one side shorter, creating a \"hook\" at the tip. In contrast, Excelsa beans are generally smaller and rounder, though also asymmetrical, averaging around 9mm long and 6mm wide.",
