      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Which one of Liberica and Excelsa is better for me?",
          "user_rubrik": "Which one of Liberica and Excelsa is better for me?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Considering your acid reflux and preference for low-acidity coffee, Excelsa beans may not be ideal as they are noted for their \"tart acidity\" (P6, P8, P12, P14). Liberica beans, while described with floral, fruity, smoky, or woody notes (P2, P12, P14) and as generally bittersweet/earthy (P1, P4), do not have this explicit mention of tartness.\n\nRegarding caffeine, Excelsa has slightly less (1g/100g) than Liberica (1.23g/100g) (P4, P17). However, prioritizing your acid reflux, Liberica seems the more suitable choice between the two.",
