      {
        "turn": 10,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "So, how does the brewing process itself change the taste of coffee?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of brewing on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The brewing process profoundly impacts coffee taste. Key factors include water temperature, which affects extraction speed and flavor compounds. Grind size influences the balance of acidity and bitterness. Brewing time dictates the extraction level, with shorter times yielding more acidity and longer times leading to bitterness or sweetness. Different brewing methods also create distinct profiles, from low-acidity cold brew to full-bodied French press. The coffee-to-water ratio and water quality further contribute to the final flavor.",
          "citations": {
