      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great info\u2014thanks! What\u2019s the best brewing method for a smooth, low-acidity coffee? I sometimes get acid reflux.",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "For a smooth, low-acidity coffee that's gentle on acid reflux, the cold brew method is highly recommended. Cold brewing uses cold or room-temperature water for a longer extraction, which results in significantly less acid being extracted compared to hot brewing. This can reduce acidity by up to 70%, making it much smoother and easier on the stomach. The Toddy coffee brew method is also an excellent cold water extraction option known to reduce oils and acidity, ideal for those with acid reflux.",
