        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That clears things up. What about different coffee bean types\u2014can you give me an overview of the main types?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Beyond Arabica and Robusta, there are two other commercially grown coffee bean species: Liberica and Excelsa. Arabica, accounting for 60-70% of global production, is prized for its sweeter, complex flavors with notes of fruit and berries, and often a bright acidity. Robusta, known for its higher caffeine, offers a bolder, harsher, and more bitter taste, often described as earthy. Liberica is rarer, primarily from Southeast Asia, known for inconsistent flavors that can be smoky, woody, or floral with a harsh finish. Excelsa, sometimes considered a Liberica variety, has a tart, fruitier profile.",
