          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "To make a really good coffee that's gentle on your stomach, consider these tips:\n\nOpt for a darker roast coffee or try cold brew, as both are generally lower in acidity. To further reduce acidity, you can add a pinch of baking soda or some almond milk to your coffee. Decaf coffee, particularly varieties processed with mountain water, can also be a good choice for lower acid content.",
