      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that's a bit better. What about brewing methods? Which one makes the smoothest cup?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "For a smoother cup that's also gentle on your stomach, cold brew is highly recommended. Its long, cold steeping process significantly reduces acidity and bitterness, resulting in a naturally sweet and smooth coffee.\n\nAnother excellent option is the Chemex pour-over. Its unique thick filters remove bitter notes and oils, producing a remarkably clean, delicate, and smooth-tasting brew. General pour-over methods also yield a smooth cup.",
