        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting, I haven't tried Chemex before. How much coffee should I use for a single mug?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "For a single mug using a Chemex, a common recommendation is to use 20 grams of coffee grounds with 300 grams of water (a 1:15 coffee-to-water ratio). Many also advise a 1:16 ratio; for example, 24 grams of coffee to 385 grams of water will yield a slightly larger cup. You can adjust the ratio to your taste.",
