      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great info! Are there any notable flavor differences between Arabica and Robusta beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Arabica beans are typically known for a sweeter, softer, and more complex flavor, often with notes of sugar, fruit, berries, nuts, or chocolate, and a pleasant acidity. Robusta beans, in contrast, generally have a bolder, harsher, and more bitter taste, frequently described with earthy, grainy, burnt, woody, or peanut-like overtones. This distinction is largely due to Arabica's higher sugar and lipid content.",
          "citations": {
