      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That explains why I tend to prefer Arabica beans. Are there any lesser-known coffee bean varieties or hybrids worth trying if I like to experiment?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are the different types of coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Given your preference for Arabica and interest in experimenting, you might enjoy exploring **Liberica** or **Excelsa** beans, which are less common. Liberica offers unique fruity, floral, and smoky notes, while Excelsa is known for a tarter profile.\n\nWithin the Arabica family, the **Gesha** variety is gaining popularity for its distinct jasmine, honeysuckle, and tropical fruit flavors. Also, **Mysore** beans from India are a soft, rich, and low-acid option.",
          "citations": {
