          "user_utterance": "That's great! Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Excelsa beans typically have a lower caffeine content, ranging from 0.86 to 1.13g per 100g, making them the lowest among common coffee types. Liberica beans have a slightly higher caffeine content at 1.23g per 100g.\n\nRegarding shape, Liberica beans are often large, irregular, and asymmetrical, sometimes described as almond-shaped with a distinctive \"hook\" at the tip. Excelsa beans are generally smaller and rounder, though they can also be asymmetrical and vary in shape and size.",
