        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Perfect! Now, what is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is the impact of roasting on coffee taste?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Roasting transforms green coffee beans by developing flavors and aromas through chemical reactions like caramelization and the Maillard reaction. It changes acidity, sweetness, and body. Lighter roasts retain more natural acidity and fruity/floral notes, while darker roasts become less acidic, more bittersweet, and can develop bolder, sometimes bitter, flavors as the roast itself becomes more prominent. Oils and volatile compounds, crucial for flavor, also migrate and can be lost over time after roasting.",
