          "user_utterance": "Nice summary! Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Short answer \u2014 both are relatively low in caffeine, but excelsa is slightly lower and the beans look different.  - Caffeine: Excelsa \u2248 0.9\u20131.1 g per 100 g (roughly 1 g/100 g); Liberica \u2248 1.2\u20131.3 g per 100 g. There\u2019s overlap and values vary with variety, growing conditions and processing, so the gap is modest.   - Shape/size: Liberica beans are larger and more almond\u2011shaped; excelsa beans tend to be smaller and rounder.  Note: taxonomy is messy\u2014excelsa is often treated close to or as a variety of liberica, so they\u2019re sometimes grouped together despite these differences. For your reflux concerns, roast level and brew method matter more than this small caffeine difference.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:6": 0.954188346862793,
            "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:13": -0.6648104190826416,
