          "user_utterance": "Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you compare the caffeine content and shape of Excelsa and Liberica coffee beans?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Short answer: they\u2019re similar \u2014 both sit closer to Arabica than Robusta in many measurements, but exact caffeine varies by variety and growing/processing conditions.  Caffeine: - Robusta ~2.0\u20132.7% (for reference). - Liberica (including many Excelsa samples) typically ~1.0\u20131.8% dry\u2011bean caffeine.   - Excelsa (often classed with Liberica) usually falls in the same general band; some cultivars register slightly lower or comparable to Liberica. Data are limited and variable, so expect overlap.  Shape: - Liberica beans are noticeably large, irregular and asymmetrical \u2014 often elongated or \u201cpear\u2011shaped\u201d with an off\u2011center crease.   - Excelsa beans (when distinguished) tend to be a bit smaller and more elongated/flattened than typical Liberica, but still more irregular than Arabica/Robusta.  Bottom line: caffeine differences are minor and inconsistent; bean shape and flavor are the clearest distinguishing features.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Which one of Liberica and Excelsa is better for me?",
          "user_rubrik": "Which one of Liberica and Excelsa is better for me?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Given your mild acid reflux and taste goals, Liberica is the safer starting pick. It\u2019s often woodier, smokier and fuller-bodied\u2014especially when darker roasted\u2014so it usually feels gentler and less bright/tart than Excelsa. Excelsa (often lumped with Liberica) tends toward tart, fruity complexity, which can be more acidic and might irritate reflux.  Practical steps: buy a small sample of Liberica (dark roast or labeled \u201clow\u2011acid\u201d), brew with a paper filter or cold brew, or use slightly lower brew temperature. If you\u2019re curious, try a tiny Excelsa sample later to compare. Track how your stomach and flavor preference respond, then iterate.",
