        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m curious about making good coffee. Any tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to make a good coffee?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Nice \u2014 since you start your day with coffee and prefer gentle beverages, try these practical tips:  - Use freshly roasted whole beans and a burr grinder; grind just before brewing.   - Match grind to method: coarse for French press, medium for drip, fine for espresso.   - Weigh coffee: try 1:15\u20131:17 coffee:water ratio (e.g., 20 g coffee \u2192 300 g water).   - Brew temp: 90\u201396\u00b0C normally; lower (\u224885\u201392\u00b0C) or cold brew (12\u201324 hrs) to reduce acidity.   - Choose dark-roast or beans labeled \u201clow-acid\u201d and use a paper filter to remove oils/acids.   - Use filtered water, rinse paper filters, and keep gear clean for consistent flavor.   - Skip sugar (you already do); add a dash of cinnamon or a small splash of milk/plant milk if reflux is an issue.   - Experiment: try Aeropress or pour-over for control. Weigh, note changes, and iterate \u2014 fits your tinkerer/dev mindset.",
